AWS Lambda Deployment: Custom Greeting Function
This repository contains the infrastructure and deployment files for a serverless AWS Lambda function created for the Nautilus DevOps team. The function returns a custom greeting with a 200 status code, demonstrating rapid deployment and scalability using AWS Lambda.

Architecture & Resources
Cloud Provider: AWS

Region: us-east-1

Service: AWS Lambda

Function Name: devops-lambda

Runtime: Python 3.11

IAM Role: lambda_execution_role (with AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole policy attached)

Function Code (lambda_function.py)
Python
import json

def lambda_handler(event, context):
    return {
        'statusCode': 200,
        'body': 'Welcome to KKE AWS Labs!'
    }
Setup & Deployment Guide
1. Create the IAM Trust Policy
Save the following trust policy configuration as trust-policy.json:

JSON
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
2. Create the IAM Role and Attach Permissions
Run the following AWS CLI commands to set up the execution role:

Bash
# Create the IAM role
aws iam create-role --role-name lambda_execution_role --assume-role-policy-document file://trust-policy.json

# Attach the basic execution policy for logs and monitoring
aws iam attach-role-policy --role-name lambda_execution_role --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole
3. Create the Deployment Package
Package the Python function into a ZIP archive:

Bash
zip function.zip lambda_function.py
4. Deploy the Lambda Function
Create the Lambda function in the us-east-1 region using the created role and deployment package:

Bash
ACCOUNT_ID=$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)

aws lambda create-function \
  --function-name devops-lambda \
  --runtime python3.11 \
  --role arn:aws:iam::${ACCOUNT_ID}:role/lambda_execution_role \
  --handler lambda_function.lambda_handler \
  --zip-file fileb://function.zip \
  --region us-east-1
Verification
Test the deployed function using the AWS CLI:

Bash
aws lambda invoke \
  --function-name devops-lambda \
  --region us-east-1 \
  response.json && cat response.json
Expected Output:

JSON
{"statusCode": 200, "body": "Welcome to KKE AWS Labs!"}
